body:
A truck full of stones appeared near the CJP protest at Jantar Mantar on July 20, prompting fears it could be used to frame protesters.

@ImAvdheshkumar traced it to a vehicle the Police had seized 4 days earlier after a crash that injured seven people.

https://t.co/5z52dbcgl4

Remember the truck full of stones that appeared near the CJP protest site in Jantar Mantar? 

@ImAvdheshkumar traced the vehicle with its registration number. It was not a stray truck: the Delhi Police had seized it four days earlier
https://t.co/weHmvyvYb0

@abhijeet_dipke "Make this protest safe for women."

— Abhijeet Dipke at Jantar Mantar.

As CJP holds its second protest, Dipke reminded supporters that a movement demanding justice must also ensure dignity, security, and inclusion for every participant. https://t.co/M4lrhx6d5d

Hindu Raksha Dal supporters arrived at Jantar Mantar against the CJP protest, Delhi Police stopped them.

@Saurabh_Unmute 

@Cockroachisback @abhijeet_dipke https://t.co/YjCP64UQao

The CJP protest at Jantar Mantar today had almost the same number of protestors. But the stage was bigger, the protest was better organised, crowd management was better, and there was free water and other arrangements.

The question arises again: who is paying for all this extravagance?

A few days ago, Rahul Gandhi did something similar in Kota. The stage was grand, but we know it was funded by his party, Congress.

So who is funding the CJP protest? Is it a party like AAP? Influencers like Dhruv Rathee? Some hidden figures from civil society? Who are they? Can we expect some transparency? 

@CJP_for_India 
@abhijeet_dipke

@abhijeet_dipke 🚨 CJP founder Abhijeet Dipke has announced a protest in Delhi on June 6.

He says he will hold a demonstration at Jantar Mantar demanding the resignation of the Education Minister over concerns surrounding the education system and accountability.

@abhijeet_dipke 
@CJP_is_back https://t.co/OFMyBQLpUK

CJP Protest खत्म, क्या फिर लौटेंगे Cockroach, प्रदर्शनकारियों ने बताया अगला प्लान

CJP | Protest | Jantar Mantar

@NehaDhiman1004 @roohanibhatia https://t.co/s5K3GsxyRy

"सरकार के लिए हम हो सकते हैं कीड़े मकौड़े, लेकिन लेकिन हम जीवित है और अपने हकों की लड़ाई लड़ने के लिए सक्षम है"

◆ CJP ने किया पोस्ट

@Cockroachisback | Cockroach Janta Party | Jantar Mantar https://t.co/mETabXavBt

This guy claims he failed his exam and is protesting due to a paper leak, but the facts tell a different story. Watch how the claim starts falling apart when checked closely.

It seems today’s narrative is getting exposed step by step. #cocroachjantaparty

@OpIndia_com ne mar rakhi hai aaj Jantar Mantar CJP protesters ki.

Cockroach Janta Party पर बड़ा अपडेट, Protest की परमिशन Delhi Police ने दे दी. 

CJP Founder Abhijeet Dipke अब सीधा Jantar Mantar पहुँच रहे. समर्थकों से भी वहीं पहुंचने की अपील.

@Saurabh_Pinch https://t.co/qw4JW7Pu52

Cockroach Janta Party announces three spokespersons who will speak on behalf of the protest movement to the public and the media. 

Investigative journalist Saurav Das will take on the role of Chief Spokesperson. Political researcher, author and filmmaker Vijeta Dahiya, and an alumnus of IIT Kanpur and the global management consulting firm McKinsey, Ashutosh Ranka, will also take on the role of Spokespersons along with Das. CJP is committed to changing the political discourse of India, and this will be led by a new generation of leaders. 

@SauravDassss @VijetaDahiya @AshutoshRanka @CJPComms
